wallet_root=(not set)

===== 1. WITHOUT wallet (expect ORA-29273 / ORA-29024) =====
NO_WALLET -> ERR -29273: ORA-29024: Certificate validation failure

===== 2. SET_WALLET('system') missing colon (expect ORA-29248) =====
system(no colon) -> ERR -29273: ORA-29248: an unrecognized WRL was used to open a wallet

===== 3. SET_WALLET('system:') -> public HTTPS hosts (system CA bundle) =====
https://www.example.com/	   OK  len=559
https://www.oracle.com/ 	   OK  len=1449
https://api.github.com/ 	   OK  len=265
https://www.cloudflare.com/	   OK  len=2000
https://www.microsoft.com/	   OK  len=2000
https://www.baidu.com/		   OK  len=1778
https://www.bing.com/		   OK  len=
https://www.gov.cn/		   OK  len=1937

===== A. system: + bogus password (expect OK -- password ignored) =====
A system:+boguspw  example.com -> OK len=559

===== B. file wallet + valid cert, TLS1.2 (expect OK) =====
B file: valid TLS1.2  -> OK len=2000

===== C. file wallet + TLS1.1-only server (expect ORA-29019 protocol version) =====
C file: TLS1.1-only  -> ERR -29273 ORA-29019: The protocol version is incorrect.

===== D. file wallet + expired server cert (expect ORA-29024 validation failure) =====
D file: expired cert -> ERR -29273 ORA-29024: Certificate validation failure

===== E. file wallet + hostname mismatch (expect ORA-24263 address mismatch) =====
E file: hostname mis -> ERR -29273 ORA-24263: remote server address on certificate and target address mismatch

===== F. system: + self-signed cert (expect ORA-29024 unknown CA) =====
F system: self-signed -> ERR -29273 ORA-29024: Certificate validation failure

===== G. toggle _allow_system_wallet (session-level -- expect ORA-02096) =====
G1 alter session -> ERR -2096 ORA-02096: specified initialization parameter is not modifiable with this option
G2 system: after toggle attempt -> OK len=559

-- Notes:
--  * len<=2000 because UTL_HTTP.REQUEST returns only the first 2000 bytes of the body.
--  * www.bing.com sometimes shows an empty body (gzip first chunk decodes empty); not a cert issue.
--  * Scenario A: the bogus password is silently ignored -- system: has no password to check.
--  * Scenario C: ORA-29019 "protocol version is incorrect" is distinct from the cert errors (ORA-29024),
--    confirming Oracle 23ai refuses to negotiate TLS1.1 (min TLS = 1.2).
--  * Scenario D: ORA-29024 is the generic cert-validation code; here the CA IS trusted (scenario B with the
--    same CA succeeded), so the only remaining reason is the expired notAfter (2020-01-01..2020-02-01).
--  * Scenario E: ORA-24263 is the specific hostname-mismatch error (cert CN/SAN lacks 127.0.0.1).
--  * Scenario G: _allow_system_wallet is NOT modifiable at session level (ORA-02096). Toggling it for real
--    needs ALTER SYSTEM ... scope=spfile + DB restart; not done here to avoid disrupting the instance.


===== Part 3: advanced experiments (captured output; shell-driven, not pure SQL) =====

--- 3.1 OS CA bundle: already-expired roots ---
ca-certificates-2024.2.69_v8.0.303-80.0.el8_10.noarch
EXPIRED: subject=C = IE, O = Baltimore, OU = CyberTrust, CN = Baltimore CyberTrust Root notAfter=May 12 23:59:00 2025 GMT
=== SUMMARY: total roots=148  already_expired=1 ===
expiring within 1 year = 3:
   Baltimore CyberTrust Root                  notAfter=2025-05 (already expired)
   Entrust Root Certification Authority       notAfter=2026-11
   Certigna                                    notAfter=2027-06

--- 3.2 clock -> 2049-01-01 (all 148 system roots past notAfter) ---
clock now: 2049-01-01 12:00:00
T1 system: example.com @2049 -> ERR -29273 ORA-29024: Certificate validation failure
=== restore clock (set-ntp true -> re-sync) ===
clock now: 2026-09-23 06:21:57
STATUS    (v$instance) -> OPEN
RESTORE system: -> OK len=559

--- 3.3 intermediate-cert expiry (file: wallet, /tmp/exproot certs) ---
expiredanchor (intermediate): subject=CN = Expired Anchor CA  notBefore=Jan 1 2019  notAfter=Jan 1 2020
chain = leaf(valid) -> expiredanchor(EXPIRED intermed) -> tempca(valid root, trusted)
I1 leaf(valid)->expiredINTERMED->validRoot -> ERR -29273 ORA-29024: Certificate validation failure
I2 leaf(valid)->validRoot(no intermed)   -> OK len=2000

-- 3.2 caveat: at clock=2049 the public leaf (1-year validity) is ALSO expired, so the ORA-29024 there
--    cannot be cleanly attributed to root expiry alone. Isolating "expired ROOT + valid leaf" is not
--    possible via system: with real public certs (leafs expire before roots; no public CA key).
--    See doc section 9 for the full analysis.


===== Part 4: parameter behavior (captured) =====

--- 4.0 metadata ---
ssl_wallet           = (null)  -- ssl_wallet
wallet_root          = (null)  -- wallet root instance initialization parameter
_implicit_ssl_wallet = TRUE    -- Implicitly use SSL Wallet for UTL_HTTP request
_allow_system_wallet = TRUE     -- Allow Usage of SYSTEM Wallet Path for Outbound Communication

--- 4.1 ssl_wallet (set at CDB$ROOT, scope=both) + _implicit_ssl_wallet=TRUE ---
set ssl_wallet=both (CDB$ROOT) -> OK ; ssl_wallet now = file:/home/oracle/wallet_http
I1 no SET_WALLET (implicit ssl_wallet) -> ERR -29273 ORA-29024: Certificate validation failure
I2 system: (ssl_wallet also set)        -> OK len=559
reset ssl_wallet -> OK ; final ssl_wallet=(null)

--- 4.2 _allow_system_wallet=FALSE (spfile + restart) ---
before: _allow_system_wallet=TRUE
set false spfile -> OK ; SHUTDOWN IMMEDIATE
STARTUP -> _allow_system_wallet=FALSE, status=OPEN
T1 system: (switch OFF) -> OK len=559     <-- switch OFF does NOT disable explicit system:
T2 file:   (switch OFF) -> OK len=559
restore: alter system set "_allow_system_wallet"=true scope=spfile -> OK ; restart
final _allow_system_wallet=TRUE, status=OPEN
VERIFY system: (switch ON) -> OK len=559

-- 4.2 conclusion: _allow_system_wallet=FALSE does NOT disable UTL_HTTP.SET_WALLET('system:').
--    The earlier claim that it is "the switch for system:" is retracted (see doc 10.4).


